<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
        <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <!-- Assembly Information -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <Version>0.8.0</Version>
        <FileVersion>0.8.0.0</FileVersion>
        <AssemblyVersion>0.8.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
        <Authors>Nandor Toth</Authors>
        <Company>Nandor Toth</Company>
        <Product>RTL-SDR Manager Library for .NET</Product>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <!-- NuGet Package Metadata -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <PackageId>RtlSdrManager</PackageId>
        <Title>RTL-SDR Manager for .NET</Title>
        <Description>A modern .NET library for managing RTL-SDR devices with support for async operations, multiple tuner types, and advanced features.</Description>
        <PackageTags>rtl-sdr;sdr;radio;rtl2832;software-defined-radio;rf;tuner</PackageTags>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/nandortoth/rtlsdr-manager</PackageProjectUrl>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/nandortoth/rtlsdr-manager</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>GPL-3.0-or-later</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2018-2026 Nandor Toth</Copyright>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <!-- NuGet Package Build Settings -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>false</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
        <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
        <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
        <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
        <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <!-- Release Notes -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>
            v0.8.0 (2026-08-15):

            ADDED:
            - SupportedFrequencyRanges on RtlSdrManagedDevice, with the TunerCapabilities,
              DemodulatorCapabilities and FrequencyRange types behind it, reporting what the
              device can currently reach: the tuner's ranges, or the ADC's while direct
              sampling is active.

            FIXED:
            - Direct sampling is usable at last. CenterFrequency validated against the tuner's
              range even while direct sampling bypassed the tuner, so every HF frequency was
              rejected. The range is now the ADC's: 0 Hz to half the crystal frequency.
            - The E4000 accepts exactly 1100 and 1250 MHz, which an asymmetric comparison
              rejected even though both are documented as supported.
            - 0.0 dB is accepted as a tuner gain on the R820T/R828D, where it is the tuner's
              lowest gain step. It was treated as an error value, so SupportedTunerGains
              reported 28 of 29 gains and TunerGain = 0.0 threw.
            - SetMaximumTunerGain()/SetMinimumTunerGain() on a tuner without manual gain
              control now name the cause, instead of throwing "Sequence contains no elements".
            - SetBiasTeeGPIO() works on every tuner, not just the R820T. The GPIO pins belong
              to the demodulator, so the restriction was never justified.

            CHANGED:
            - BREAKING: reading TunerGain, CenterFrequency or SampleRate before one has been
              set throws InvalidOperationException instead of RtlSdrLibraryExecutionException.
              All three reported a device failure for what is a usage error.
            - Enabling direct sampling resets the center frequency to 0 Hz when the current one
              is beyond the ADC's reach, because the demodulator would truncate it silently.
            - BREAKING: SetBiasTeeGPIO() throws ArgumentOutOfRangeException for a pin outside
              0..7, instead of RtlSdrLibraryExecutionException.
            - SetMinimumTunerGain() selects 0.0 dB on the R820T/R828D instead of 0.9 dB.
            - The E4000's 1100 to 1250 MHz gap is no longer rejected up front: its boundaries
              vary between devices, so the tuner decides and reports the outcome.

            See CHANGELOG.md for complete details and previous releases.
        </PackageReleaseNotes>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <!-- Package Icon -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <PackageIcon>RtlSdrManager.Icon.128.png</PackageIcon>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="../../design/icon/RtlSdrManager.Icon.128.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <!-- Include README in package -->
    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <!-- Source Link Support (for debugging) -->
    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <!-- Expose internals to the unit test project -->
    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="RtlSdrManager.Tests" />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
